<h1>Managing Submissions</h1>

<p>
    Submissions are how you track quotes from different carriers and wholesalers for a renewal. Each submission represents one quote or application you're pursuing. Think of submissions as your way of keeping track of all the options you're exploring for a client.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the submissions grid/table showing multiple submissions with different statuses (Created, Quoted, Proposed, Bound) organized by wholesaler groups. Show the visual layout and status indicators. -->

<h2>What is a Submission?</h2>

<p>
    A submission represents a quote request or application you've sent to a carrier (either directly or through a wholesaler). For each renewal, you might create multiple submissions as you shop around for the best coverage and price.
</p>

<p>
    Each submission tracks:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Which carrier</strong> you're getting a quote from</li>
    <li><strong>Which wholesaler</strong> (if any) is helping you access that carrier</li>
    <li><strong>The status</strong> of the quote (created, submitted, quoted, proposed, bound, etc.)</li>
    <li><strong>The premium</strong> the carrier quoted</li>
    <li><strong>Important dates</strong> like when you submitted and when you received the quote</li>
    <li><strong>Contacts</strong> at the carrier or wholesaler handling this submission</li>
    <li><strong>Attachments</strong> like the quote document, application, or related emails</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of a single submission detail view or expanded row showing all the fields mentioned above. Use callouts or labels to identify each piece of information. -->

<h2>Creating a Submission</h2>

<p>
    To create a new submission for a renewal:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Open the renewal you're working on</li>
    <li>Go to the <strong>Submissions</strong> section</li>
    <li>Click the <strong>Create New</strong> button (or "Add Submission")</li>
    <li>Fill in the details:
        <ul>
            <li>Select the carrier you're submitting to</li>
            <li>If going through a wholesaler, select the wholesaler</li>
            <li>Choose the product type (General Liability, Workers' Comp, etc.)</li>
            <li>Add any notes about special requirements or instructions</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Save the submission</li>
</ol>

<p>
    The system will automatically set the initial status to "Created" and you can update it as the submission progresses.
</p>

