<h2>Understanding Submission Status</h2>

<p>
    Submissions move through several statuses as you work with carriers. Here's what each status means:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Created</strong> – You've created the submission but haven't started working on it yet</li>
    <li><strong>Started</strong> – You've begun preparing the submission (gathering documents, filling out applications)</li>
    <li><strong>Submitted</strong> – You've sent the application or quote request to the carrier/wholesaler</li>
    <li><strong>Quoted</strong> – The carrier has provided a quote</li>
    <li><strong>Proposed</strong> – You've sent this quote to the client as part of a proposal</li>
    <li><strong>Bound</strong> – The client has accepted this quote and you've bound the coverage</li>
    <li><strong>Declined</strong> – The carrier declined to quote or the client declined this option</li>
    <li><strong>Rejected</strong> – The quote was rejected for some reason</li>
</ul>

<p>
    You can update the status by clicking on the status stepper or using the status dropdown. Some statuses update automatically—for example, when you send a proposal, the leading submission will be marked as "Proposed."
</p>

